"""openFDA device/pma fixtures — real records from the bulk export (2026-08-03).

Every awkward shape this parser must survive is a REAL record, chosen by
measurement rather than invented:

  * an original application, decision APPR, Class 3 — the easy case.
  * an original with APWD ("Withdrawal after approval") — approved and THEN
    withdrawn, which is not the same fact as never approved.
  * an original with APCB, a code the FDA data dictionary does not define at all
    (11 records live). It must render as undocumented, never as an approval.
  * a supplement with OK30 — also undocumented, and 27,693 records, 49% of the
    whole source.
  * THE TRAP: a supplement whose `supplement_type` is EMPTY but whose
    `supplement_number` is real. 1,885 such records exist. Keying originals off
    supplement_type counts 3,358 originals where there are 1,473 — a 128%
    overstatement of the approval base.
  * a Class 2 PMA, because 7,177 of them exist and "PMA implies Class III" is
    wrong on 14% of the source.

DEVICE_PMA_BULK_ZIP is the same payload as a real zip, so bulk.py's download →
unzip → parse → completeness path is exercised against real bytes with no network.
"""

